1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,706
A disposition is the outcome of an activity, such as No answer, Call

2
00:00:05,706 --> 00:00:07,613
back, or Not interested.

3
00:00:07,613 --> 00:00:12,891
This video shows why dispositions exist, how to create them, how outcomes let

4
00:00:12,891 --> 00:00:16,770
the platform apply them for you, and what happens next.

5
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:24,480
Every call, text or task ends in some way.

6
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,080
The customer did not answer, asked for a call back, booked a test

7
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:32,190
drive, or asked not to be contacted again.

8
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:37,969
Agents pick that answer when they complete an activity, and an AI conversation

9
00:00:37,969 --> 00:00:39,705
picks one when it ends.

10
00:00:39,705 --> 00:00:41,800
That answer is a disposition.

11
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:45,531
The disposition is what drives the rest.

12
00:00:45,531 --> 00:00:49,095
The subject flow decides what each one does next:

13
00:00:49,095 --> 00:00:52,530
finish, try again later, or create a follow-up.

14
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:59,540
Reports use dispositions too, so a manager can see how many calls ended in each outcome.

15
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:07,633
Open Interaction Center, Management, Dispositions.

16
00:01:07,633 --> 00:01:09,530
Click Add Disposition.

17
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:15,678
Enter a Name.

18
00:01:15,678 --> 00:01:17,365
Names must be unique.

19
00:01:17,365 --> 00:01:23,801
Add a Description, because a clear description helps agents, and the AI, tell the outcomes apart.

20
00:01:24,256 --> 00:01:28,954
Outcome stays None for a disposition that only people or the AI pick.

21
00:01:28,954 --> 00:01:31,397
Set lead status is for lead work:

22
00:01:31,397 --> 00:01:36,471
when an activity that belongs to a lead is completed with this disposition,

23
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:38,726
the lead moves to that status.

24
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:40,230
Click Save.

25
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:43,743
A test-drive campaign might use three dispositions:

26
00:01:43,743 --> 00:01:47,442
Test Drive Booked, Call Back Later and Not Interested.

27
00:01:47,937 --> 00:01:52,804
The other two are created the same way, with a name and a description.

28
00:01:52,804 --> 00:01:57,607
The list then shows all three, each with an Edit and a Delete button.

29
00:02:01,907 --> 00:02:03,903
Open a disposition again.

30
00:02:03,903 --> 00:02:07,251
After it is saved, its name cannot be changed.

31
00:02:07,251 --> 00:02:09,247
Only its description can.

32
00:02:12,261 --> 00:02:17,416
Deleting a disposition does not check whether a subject flow still uses it.

33
00:02:17,416 --> 00:02:19,771
Remove it from the flows first.

34
00:02:23,971 --> 00:02:28,556
Set an Outcome only on a disposition the platform should apply on its

35
00:02:28,556 --> 00:02:31,612
own, when a call ends in a way nobody chose.

36
00:02:31,612 --> 00:02:34,241
Leave it at None for everything else.

37
00:02:34,991 --> 00:02:39,280
Number not in service adds the called number to the Numbers Not In

38
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:42,735
Service list, so it is never loaded or dialed again.

39
00:02:42,735 --> 00:02:47,500
No answer, Busy and Answering machine cover calls that were not picked up,

40
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:50,061
by the dialer and by automated calls.

41
00:02:50,811 --> 00:02:55,478
Rejected and Call failed are for calls the network declined or failed.

42
00:02:55,478 --> 00:03:00,084
Disconnected is for a customer who hung up before an agent joined, or

43
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:03,031
before an automated call decided anything.

44
00:03:03,781 --> 00:03:07,952
The dialer applies these to every call that ends before an agent is

45
00:03:07,952 --> 00:03:10,981
connected, so the agent never sees those calls.

46
00:03:12,587 --> 00:03:18,757
Here, a disposition named Number Not In Service gets the outcome Number not in service.

47
00:03:25,333 --> 00:03:29,462
A second one, named No Answer, gets the outcome No answer.

48
00:03:29,462 --> 00:03:33,656
The list shows each outcome as a badge next to the name, so

49
00:03:33,656 --> 00:03:36,753
the dialer knows which disposition to use.

50
00:03:40,953 --> 00:03:45,080
When the platform needs a disposition for an outcome, it uses the one

51
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:49,592
with that outcome in the activity's subject flow, so the flow's actions run,

52
00:03:49,592 --> 00:03:51,683
such as Try Again for No answer.

53
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:57,216
If the flow has none, it falls back to another disposition with that

54
00:03:57,216 --> 00:03:59,220
outcome, or to No answer.

55
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:03,874
If there is still none, it creates one, such as No Answer or Busy.

56
00:04:03,874 --> 00:04:08,012
A created disposition is in no flow, so add it to the flow

57
00:04:08,012 --> 00:04:10,533
to have the contact called again.

58
00:04:11,283 --> 00:04:16,310
A disposition only appears on an activity's Complete page when the subject flow

59
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,907
has an action for it.

60
00:04:17,907 --> 00:04:21,396
To mark a contact Do Not Call, use Set do not call on

61
00:04:21,396 --> 00:04:24,413
the disposition's action in the subject flow.

62
00:04:28,613 --> 00:04:33,554
A test-drive campaign uses Test Drive Booked, Call Back Later and Not Interested,

63
00:04:33,554 --> 00:04:36,053
so reports show how the campaign went.

64
00:04:36,803 --> 00:04:40,859
A dead number is marked for you, once a disposition has the Number

65
00:04:40,859 --> 00:04:42,493
not in service outcome.

66
00:04:43,243 --> 00:04:47,504
A disposition that sets a lead status keeps the lead's stage up to

67
00:04:47,504 --> 00:04:50,463
date, without the agent changing it by hand.

68
00:04:52,463 --> 00:04:57,440
Create the outcomes, give the automatic ones an outcome, and let the subject

69
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,625
flow decide what happens next.

70
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:01,203
Thanks for watching.

